 Because `frai-core` is a regular ESM package, you can import only the modules you need and embed FRAI capabilities inside automation pipelines, CI jobs, or custom products.
 
+### Evaluation with Thresholds
+
+The `Eval` module supports metric thresholds to gate evaluation results. Pass a `thresholds` object to `generateReport`:
+
+```ts
+import { Eval } from 'frai-core';
+
+const evaluations = Eval.runEvaluations({
+  outputs: ['hello', 'world'],
+  references: ['hello', 'world']
+});
+
+const report = Eval.generateReport({
+  evaluations,
+  outputsPath: './outputs.json',
+  referencesPath: './references.json',
+  thresholds: {
+    exact_match: 0.9,
+    toxicity: 0.95
+  }
+});
+
+console.log(report.passed); // true if all thresholds passed, false otherwise
+console.log(report.thresholds); // array of threshold results with { metric, min, score, passed }
+```
+
+Thresholds pass when a metric's score is at least the minimum. Metrics with no score (e.g., exact match without references) fail their threshold. Reports are written regardless of threshold outcome.
+
